---
// The four experience beats. This is the neutral copy rendered server-side so
// no-JS visitors get a complete page. The personalization controller in
// workshop.astro rewrites every card's title + body to the visitor's chosen
// lens (healing / freedom / professional) — see the CARDS map there.
const items = [
  {
    title: 'An introduction to Somatic Vocal Healing',
    body: 'The method where sound becomes the language of the body — a closer connection to your body, your own sound, and whatever wants to show up underneath.',
  },
  {
    title: 'A somatic warm-up with live piano',
    body: 'So your nervous system can arrive before anything else happens — settling, breath widening, listening getting finer.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Guided sounding',
    body: "A somatic practice for giving what's here a sound — not describing it, sounding it. The healing is in the acknowledgment. And a little more trust in speaking your own truth, at home and at work.",
  },
  {
    title: 'A first tool for everyday life',
    body: 'Something to keep coming back to — when something in you is stuck, when your head is too loud, when the day has made you shut down. You can keep practising it on your own after.',
  },
];
---

<section class="we-what" id="workshop">
  <div class="we-what-inner">
    <div class="we-what-head">
      <div class="we-eyebrow">What to expect</div>
      <h2 class="we-h2">
        One hour —<br />
        and a <em>different way in</em> to yourself.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="we-what-intro">
      <p>
        Somatic Vocal Healing is a somatic practice: you use your own voice to
        feel what's here and give it expression. Singing is its own beautiful
        art — this is something quieter and more inward. Your voice becomes a
        way to meet what's alive in you, and the crackle, the wobble, the little
        break in the throat all belong, because they carry information.
      </p>
      <p>
        In this hour I'll introduce you to the method, gently. You'll sound.
        You'll feel. You'll notice that your body has been waiting a long time
        for a language that doesn't come from the head.
      </p>
      <p>You don't need a good voice. You need your honest one.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="we-what-sub">What you'll experience</div>
    <div class="we-what-grid">
      {
        items.map((it, i) => (
          <article class="we-what-card">
            <div class="we-what-num">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</div>
            <h3 class="we-what-card-title we-swap" id={`we-card-title-${i}`}>{it.title}</h3>
            <p class="we-what-card-body we-swap" id={`we-card-body-${i}`}>{it.body}</p>
          </article>
        ))
      }
    </div>

    <p class="we-what-coffee">
      One hour only opens the door. But it's enough to feel that this is real —
      and to leave with a practice you can keep for
      <em>the rest of your life.</em>
    </p>
    <p class="we-what-coffee-foot">
      One hour. <span data-sd-price="ticket">22€</span>. That's deliberate — <em>the door should be easy to open.</em>
    </p>

    <div class="we-what-cta-wrap">
      <a href="#register" class="we-link-cta">
        Register for the next workshop <i class="ph-light ph-arrow-right"></i>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
